<http://data.silknow.org/object/d00a37fa-9f18-39d7-a44d-85a020c4443e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Set of five silk and pashmina carpet fragments. Silk warps and wefts and pashmina (goat-hair) pile. With a design of trees and flowers on a deep red ground.\n\nSilk warp, S plied and Z spun. Cream, red or green in various parts of the fragment. The threads lie on two levels. About 50 to an inch.\n\nWeft of red silk one shoot.\nWoollen pile.\nPersian knot, about 25 horizontally to the inch. About 24 vertically, ie. 600 to square inch approx."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d00a37fa-9f18-39d7-a44d-85a020c4443e> .

